@anon.3c5d4856225436a016f648d8ca8332b3.2050 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [1147 x i8] }> <{ [1147 x i8] c"# `abi_msp430_interrupt`\0A\0AThe tracking issue for this feature is: [#38487]\0A\0A[#38487]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/38487\0A\0A------------------------\0A\0AIn the MSP430 architecture, interrupt handlers have a special calling\0Aconvention. You can use the `\22msp430-interrupt\22` ABI to make the compiler apply\0Athe right calling convention to the interrupt handlers you define.\0A\0A<!-- NOTE(ignore) this example is specific to the msp430 target -->\0A\0A``` rust,ignore\0A#![feature(abi_msp430_interrupt)]\0A#![no_std]\0A\0A// Place the interrupt handler at the appropriate memory address\0A// (Alternatively, you can use `#[used]` and remove `pub` and `#[no_mangle]`)\0A#[link_section = \22__interrupt_vector_10\22]\0A#[no_mangle]\0Apub static TIM0_VECTOR: extern \22msp430-interrupt\22 fn() = tim0;\0A\0A// The interrupt handler\0Aextern \22msp430-interrupt\22 fn tim0() {\0A    // ..\0A}\0A```\0A\0A``` text\0A$ msp430-elf-objdump -CD ./target/msp430/release/app\0ADisassembly of section __interrupt_vector_10:\0A\0A0000fff2 <TIM0_VECTOR>:\0A    fff2:       00 c0           interrupt service routine at 0xc000\0A\0ADisassembly of section .text:\0A\0A0000c000 <int::tim0>:\0A    c000:       00 13           reti\0A```\0A" }>, align 1
