@anon.3c5d4856225436a016f648d8ca8332b3.2108 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [13290 x i8] }> <{ [13290 x i8] c"# `asm_experimental_arch`\0A\0AThe tracking issue for this feature is: [#93335]\0A\0A[#93335]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/93335\0A\0A------------------------\0A\0AThis feature tracks `asm!` and `global_asm!` support for the following architectures:\0A- NVPTX\0A- PowerPC\0A- Hexagon\0A- MIPS32r2 and MIPS64r2\0A- wasm32\0A- BPF\0A- SPIR-V\0A- AVR\0A- MSP430\0A- M68k\0A- CSKY\0A- s390x\0A\0A## Register classes\0A\0A| Architecture | Register class | Registers                          | LLVM constraint code |\0A| ------------ | -------------- | ---------------------------------- | -------------------- |\0A| MIPS         | `reg`          | `$[2-25]`                          | `r`                  |\0A| MIPS         | `freg`         | `$f[0-31]`                         | `f`                  |\0A| NVPTX        | `reg16`        | None\\*                             | `h`                  |\0A| NVPTX        | `reg32`        | None\\*                             | `r`                  |\0A| NVPTX        | `reg64`        | None\\*                             | `l`                  |\0A| Hexagon      | `reg`          | `r[0-28]`                          | `r`                  |\0A| PowerPC      | `reg`          | `r[0-31]`                          | `r`                  |\0A| PowerPC      | `reg_nonzero`  | `r[1-31]`                          | `b`                  |\0A| PowerPC      | `freg`         | `f[0-31]`                          | `f`                  |\0A| PowerPC      | `cr`           | `cr[0-7]`, `cr`                    | Only clobbers        |\0A| PowerPC      | `xer`          | `xer`                              | Only clobbers        |\0A| wasm32       | `local`        | None\\*                             | `r`                  |\0A| BPF          | `reg`          | `r[0-10]`                          | `r`                  |\0A| BPF          | `wreg`         | `w[0-10]`                          | `w`                  |\0A| AVR          | `reg`          | `r[2-25]`, `XH`, `XL`, `ZH`, `ZL`  | `r`                  |\0A| AVR          | `reg_upper`    | `r[16-25]`, `XH`, `XL`, `ZH`, `ZL` | `d`                  |\0A| AVR          | `reg_pair`     | `r3r2` .. `r25r24`, `X`, `Z`       | `r`                  |\0A| AVR          | `reg_iw`       | `r25r24`, `X`, `Z`                 | `w`                  |\0A| AVR          | `reg_ptr`      | `X`, `Z`                           | `e`                  |\0A| MSP430       | `reg`          | `r[0-15]`                          | `r`                  |\0A| M68k         | `reg`          | `d[0-7]`, `a[0-7]`                 | `r`                  |\0A| M68k         | `reg_data`     | `d[0-7]`                           | `d`                  |\0A| M68k         | `reg_addr`     | `a[0-3]`                           | `a`                  |\0A| CSKY         | `reg`          | `r[0-31]`                          | `r`                  |\0A| CSKY         | `freg`         | `f[0-31]`                          | `f`                  |\0A| s390x        | `reg`          | `r[0-10]`, `r[12-14]`              | `r`                  |\0A| s390x        | `freg`         | `f[0-15]`                          | `f`                  |\0A\0A> **Notes**:\0A> - NVPTX doesn't have a fixed register set, so named registers are not supported.\0A>\0A> - WebAssembly doesn't have registers, so named registers are not supported.\0A\0A# Register class supported types\0A\0A| Architecture | Register class                  | Target feature | Allowed types                           |\0A| ------------ | ------------------------------- | -------------- | --------------------------------------- |\0A| MIPS32       | `reg`                           | None           | `i8`, `i16`, `i32`, `f32`               |\0A| MIPS32       | `freg`                          | None           | `f32`, `f64`                         