                                                                                                                                               |\0A| MIPS         | `$28`/`$gp`                             | Global pointer cannot be used as inputs or outputs.                                                                                                                                 |\0A| MIPS         | `$ra`                                   | Return address cannot be used as inputs or outputs.                                                                                                                                 |\0A| Hexagon      | `lr`                                    | This is the link register which cannot be used as an input or output.                                                                                                               |\0A| AVR          | `r0`, `r1`, `r1r0`                      | Due to an issue in LLVM, the `r0` and `r1` registers cannot be used as inputs or outputs.  If modified, they must be restored to their original values before the end of the block. |\0A|MSP430        | `r0`, `r2`, `r3`                        | These are the program counter, status register, and constant generator respectively. Neither the status register nor constant generator can be written to.                          |\0A| M68k         | `a4`, `a5`                              | Used internally by LLVM for the base pointer and global base pointer. |\0A| CSKY         | `r7`, `r28`                             | Used internally by LLVM for the base pointer and global base pointer. |\0A| CSKY         | `r8`                                    | Used internally by LLVM for the frame pointer. |\0A| CSKY         | `r14`                                   | Used internally by LLVM for the stack pointer. |\0A| CSKY         | `r15`                                   | This is the link register. |\0A| CSKY         | `r[26-30]`                              | Reserved by its ABI.       |\0A| CSKY         | `r31`                                   | This is the TLS register.  |\0A\0A\0A## Template modifiers\0A\0A| Architecture | Register class | Modifier | Example output | LLVM modifier |\0A| ------------ | -------------- | -------- | -------------- | ------------- |\0A| MIPS         | `reg`          | None     | `$2`           | None          |\0A| MIPS         | `freg`         | None     | `$f0`          | None          |\0A| NVPTX        | `reg16`        | None     | `rs0`          | None          |\0A| NVPTX        | `reg32`        | None     | `r0`           | None          |\0A| NVPTX        | `reg64`        | None     | `rd0`          | None          |\0A| Hexagon      | `reg`          | None     | `r0`           | None          |\0A| PowerPC      | `reg`          | None     | `0`            | None          |\0A| PowerPC      | `reg_nonzero`  | None     | `3`            | None          |\0A| PowerPC      | `freg`         | None     | `0`            | None          |\0A| s390x        | `reg`          | None     | `%r0`          | None          |\0A| s390x        | `reg_addr`     | None     | `%r1`          | None          |\0A| s390x        | `freg`         | None     | `%f0`          | None          |\0A| CSKY         | `reg`          | None     | `r0`           | None          |\0A| CSKY         | `freg`         | None     | `f0`           | None          |\0A\0A# Flags covered by `preserves_flags`\0A\0AThese flags registers must be restored upon exiting the asm block if the `preserves_flags` option is set:\0A- AVR\0A  - The status register `SREG`.\0A- MSP430\0A  - The status register `r2`.\0A- M68k\0A  - The condition code register `ccr`.\0A- s390x\0A  - The condition code register `cc`.\0A" }>, align 1
