@anon.3c5d4856225436a016f648d8ca8332b3.2493 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [2282 x i8] }> <{ [2282 x i8] c"# `diagnostic_namespace`\0A\0AThe tracking issue for this feature is: [#111996]\0A\0A[#111996]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/111996\0A\0A------------------------\0A\0AThe `diagnostic_namespace` feature permits customization of compilation errors.\0A\0A## diagnostic::on_unimplemented\0A\0AWith [#114452] support for `diagnostic::on_unimplemented` was added.\0A\0AWhen used on a trait declaration, the following options are available:\0A\0A* `message` to customize the primary error message\0A* `note` to add a customized note message to an error message\0A* `label` to customize the label part of the error message\0A\0AThe attribute will hint to the compiler to use these in error messages:\0A```rust\0A// some library\0A#![feature(diagnostic_namespace)]\0A\0A#[diagnostic::on_unimplemented(\0A    message = \22cannot insert element\22,\0A    label = \22cannot be put into a table\22,\0A    note = \22see <link> for more information about the Table api\22\0A)]\0Apub trait Element {\0A    // ...\0A}\0A```\0A\0A```rust,compile_fail,E0277\0A# #![feature(diagnostic_namespace)]\0A#\0A# #[diagnostic::on_unimplemented(\0A#    message = \22cannot insert element\22,\0A#    label = \22cannot be put into a table\22,\0A#    note = \22see <link> for more information about the Table api\22\0A# )]\0A# pub trait Element {\0A#    // ...\0A# }\0A# struct Table;\0A# impl Table {\0A#    fn insert<T: Element>(&self, element: T) {\0A#        // ..\0A#    }\0A# }\0A# fn main() {\0A#    let table = Table;\0A#    let element = ();\0A// user code\0Atable.insert(element);\0A# }\0A```\0A\0A```text\0Aerror[E0277]: cannot insert element\0A  --> src/main.rs:24:18\0A   |\0A24 |     table.insert(element);\0A   |           ------ ^^^^^^^ cannot be put into a table\0A   |           |\0A   |           required by a bound introduced by this call\0A   |\0A   = help: the trait `Element` is not im